name c01m07-spiritual-reclamation
timeout 600
time 1992-10-29T05:08:00Z

# COMANCHE: MAXIMUM OVERKILL (NovaLogic 1992), CAMPAIGN ONE "OPERATION MAXIMUM OVERKILL",
# MISSION 7 OF 10 -- {Spiritual Reclamation}* [MIS].
# Spec, provenance and every open question: mods/comanche/doc/campaign.md, terrain.md,
# substitutions.md, hud.md. Format: doc/missions/syntax.md.
#
# THE TASK [MIS]: 11 goals -- 3 T-80s, 3 Geckos and 5 Werewolves -- flown ALONE ("you fly into
# battle alone with a minimal complement of weapons"), on 6 000 fuel, with 8 artillery calls that this
# tree cannot express at all.
#
# THE FIELD [MIS]: map 1 (Alto Mayo, Peru, terrain.md 6), night -- sun -70.05 deg at the lead's
# spawn, computed by the runner. 11 starred objects, unlock marker *.
# THE CAST: 5 Werewolf -> `ah64` - 9 T-80 -> `target_hard` - 3 Gecko -> `sa8`.
# THE LOADOUT [MIS]: cannon 500, rockets 62, Hellfire 6, Stinger 10, artillery 8, wingman 0, fuel
# 6000. Declared here: 4 x `mk82`, 4 x `aim9`, gun 500, `set fuel_int_pct 30` = 6000 against the
# campaign's own maximum of 20 000. The rockets and the artillery have no row and no mechanism;
# the truncation of the other two is the F-16's nine pylons.

# ---- THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES ARE STATED IN FULL IN c01m01-werewolves-on-patrol.fbm AND APPLY HERE
# ---- UNCHANGED: D1 no rotorcraft (the RAH-66 flies as `module f16`, 300 kt because 180-275 kt crash
# ---- the egress) - D2 the Werewolf is an `ah64` mover and fires nothing, ever - D3 flat 0 m ground,
# ---- because one mod carries one DEM and this campaign needs four theatres - D4 the clock is checked
# ---- against the logged sun elevation - D5 the anchoring is terrain.md's reconstruction and the
# ---- campaign names no place - D6 the striker spawns on the bearing to its aim point, because the
# ---- attack phase cannot fly itself onto its own run-in - D7 one striker is one aim point.
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `lead`'s, and it flies ALONE.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires the 11 goals, alone, on 6 000 fuel, with 8 artillery calls. This is the
#   campaign's only mission where artillery is load-bearing, so a run that never calls artillery and
#   still wins means the artillery model is UNTESTED, not that it works. MEASURED: there is no
#   artillery model to test -- no off-map fire support of any kind exists in this tree -- so the
#   mission's own premise is absent and its verdict says nothing about the original's balance.
#   exit 3 = the expected reading; report the met count against 11.

# MEASURED (exit 3, `--elev const`): TWO OF ELEVEN, from ONE bomb.
#   t = 21.3 s          one Mk-82 away, aimErrM 5.07 -- and FOUR objects die (t01, t02, t03, g01), all
#                       four stacked on cell 690,475. Two of the four are goals; the other two are not,
#                       and the difference is invisible to the weapon
#   verdict             `lead` TIMEOUT, 2 of 11 met, `survive` met. 12 SA-8 launches, no hit.
#   THE ARTILLERY IS ABSENT, not unused: 8 calls declared by the game, 0 declarable here.

unit lead
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight m07 1
  spawn -5.99413 -76.94731 150 185.8 300
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 30
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk82
  set store 4 mk82
  set store 6 mk82
  set store 7 mk82
  set store 1 aim9
  set store 2 aim9
  set store 8 aim9
  set store 9 aim9
  set gun_rounds 500
  set cmds_mode auto
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp -6.02967 -76.95092 150 300
  wp -6.06548 -76.95456 1000 300
  objective kill unit t02
  objective kill unit g01
  objective kill unit t05
  objective kill unit g02
  objective kill unit t08
  objective kill unit g03
  objective kill unit w01
  objective kill unit w02
  objective kill unit w03
  objective kill unit w04
  objective kill unit w05
  objective survive

unit t01
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn -6.02967 -76.95092 ground 0.0 0

